19:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"LESSON 02 OF 10"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Capacity, throughput, and tail latency"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Throughput"}]," is work completed per unit time; ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"latency"}]," is elapsed time for one request. More throughput does not imply a good user experience if the slowest requests become much slower. A capacity estimate is an initial model to test, not a procurement order."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"calculate-from-demand-to-peak","children":"Calculate from demand to peak"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["Suppose the library receives ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"10 million document opens/day"}]," and ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"100,000 edits/day"}],". Average opens are ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"10,000,000 / 86,400 ≈ 116 requests/second"}],". If the busiest period is ten times the average, plan an initial ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"1,160 open requests/second"}],", plus edits and search. State the multiplier as an assumption and verify it from traffic telemetry. A 2× seasonal event or retry storm may require a separate scenario."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":["If one open occupies an API worker for 120 ms, Little's law gives roughly ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"1,160 × 0.120 ≈ 139"}]," concurrent in-flight opens at that peak. This is a first concurrency estimate; queues, I/O wait, connection pools, and burst shape still matter. If each open causes three database queries, the database sees roughly 3,480 queries/second before cache hits. Measure the real fanout."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"know-what-p99-measures","children":"Know what p99 measures"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"A p99 of 400 ms means 99% of requests in the measured population finish at or below 400 ms; 1% take longer. With 10 million opens/day, that remaining 1% is still about 100,000 slow opens. Segment by endpoint, region, tenant, payload size, and result; one aggregate percentile can hide a painful subgroup. Percentiles of stages cannot simply be added to obtain end-to-end p99 because the slow requests may differ across stages."}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":"Set a rough budget: edge and network 70 ms, API work 60 ms, database 120 ms, object retrieval 100 ms, headroom 50 ms. The pieces add to 400 ms as a planning envelope, not a guarantee. Verify with end-to-end traces under representative load, especially when concurrent requests compete for connections."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"diagram-load-concurrency-and-tail","children":"Diagram: load, concurrency, and tail"}],"\n",["$","figure","p-5",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/scale-design/capacity.svg","alt":"Average demand rises tenfold at peak, increasing concurrent requests and making the p99 tail visible.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"Average demand rises tenfold at peak, increasing concurrent requests and making the p99 tail visible."}]]}],"\n",["$","details","pre-0",{"className":"docs_textDiagram__KfHuf","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Read the text version of this flow"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-aosdf-diagram","children":"10M opens/day ÷ 86,400 ≈ 116 average RPS\nPeak assumption ×10 ≈ 1,160 RPS\nIn-flight estimate = 1,160 RPS × 0.12 s ≈ 139\n"}]}]]}],"\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31"],false]}]]}],"$L32"]}]
